[00:16.50]gleam v. 闪烁；（眼睛）表露出，流露出‖n. 微光；少量；（感情的）表露 示例 ① In English, many words talking about light start with "gl"—glitter, glow, gleam, glisten and so on. 在英语中，很多表达“光”的词都是以“gl”开头的，如：glitter （闪光）, glow（暗淡的光）, gleam（微光）, glisten（发光） 等。（www.worth.com） ② Her eyes gleamed with amusement at the sight of the beautiful dress. 一看到这件漂亮的裙子，她眼睛里就流露出愉悦的神情。
[00:25.30]sum n. 金额，款项；总数‖v. 概括；估量， 判断 示例 ① There are few more sobering online activities than entering data into college-tuition calculators and gasping as the Web spits back a six-figure sum. 把数据输入到大学学费计算器中，当页面弹出一个六位数时，让人不由地倒吸一口气——没有什么网上活动比这个更令人惊醒了。（2009. 6）② She was good at sums when she was a child. 她小时候擅长算术。
[00:33.11]shaft n. 一道（光、阳光等）；一阵（疼痛、 害怕等） 示例 ① Gravity Power, a start-up based in California, has devised a system that relies on two water-filled shafts, one wider than the other, which are connected at both ends. 从加州起家的重力发电公司设计出一个（储能）系统，该系统依靠两个注满水的竖井，其中一个比另外一个要宽一些，两个注水井在底部相连。（The Economist）② Shafts of fear ran through him as he heard footsteps behind him on a cold night. 在一个寒冷的夜里，他听见身后有脚步声，这让他感到一阵毛骨悚然。
[00:42.16]context n.（事情发生的）背景，环境；上下文，语境 示例 ① But schools rarely dig down to find out what really makes an applicant succeed, to create a class which also contains diversity of attitude and approach—arguably the only diversity that, in a business context, really matters. 但是学校很少刨根问底地去挖掘真正使申请人获得成功的因素，也没有潜下心来创造一个包含多样观念和方法的课堂——有理由说，在商业环境中，观念和方法的多样性才是唯一重要的多样性。（2011. 6）② You should guess the meaning of new words from the context when you do some reading. 当你阅读时，应该根据上下文猜出生词的含义。
[00:50.22]entity n. 独立存在物，实体 示例 ① Over time he might become his own entity. 随着时间的流逝，他有可能会变成独特的个体。（2010. 6）② With the development of the economy of the world, these countries can no longer be viewed as single entities. 随着世界经济的发展，这些国家不可能再被看成是单一实体。
[01:00.23]fantasy n. 幻想；幻想作品 示例 ① It has a bit of everything: fantasy, magic, adventure, and chilling fear in moments. 它把幻想、魔法、冒险和瞬时间的胆战心惊都糅合在了一起。（The Guardian）② It is advisable for her to stop living in a fantasy world. 对她来说， 不再生活在幻想世界中是很明智的。
[01:07.18]miniature a. 很小的，微型的‖n. 小画像；微缩模型 示例 ① I shrugged feigning innocence as I slid one hand into my pocket to check that the crumpled miniature was still there. 我耸了耸肩，装出一副清白无辜的样子，同时把一只手滑进口袋查看了一下，发现那张皱巴巴的小画像还在。（The Guardian）② She enjoys a doll's house with everything in miniature. 她喜欢样样东西都很小的玩具小房子。 语料 A day is a miniature of eternity. 一天是永恒的缩影。（美国作家爱默生）
[01:15.18]attribute n. 属性，特征‖ v. 把…归因于；认为是…所为（或说、写、 作） 示例 ① They may have particular attributes, like being able to talk! 它们可能具有特殊的属性，比如能够讲话。（The Guardian）② He attributes his success to hard work, the support of his family and a little luck. 他将成功归功于努力、家人的支持和一点点运气。
[01:26.70]modify v. 调整；缓和；修饰 示例 ① Is the experience of having a charismatic black president modifying lingering racist attitudes? 经历了这位有魅力的黑人总统，存在已久的种族主义态度是否会改变呢？（2010. 6） ② The management system has been modified over the years. 这套管理系统经过了多年的改进。
[01:34.33]curb v. 控制，抑制，限制‖n. 起控制（或限制）作用的事物；路边 示例 ① That conclusion was reinforced by another finding: that their opposition appeared to soften when that fiscal burden decreased, as occurred with welfare reform in the 1990s, which curbed immigrants' access to certain benefits. 另一项发现更进一步证实了这一结论——20世纪90年代的福利改革限制了移民获得某些福利，从而使财政负担减小，这时，反对者们的态度也缓和了。（2011. 6）② It is crucial for her to learn to curb her bad temper. 学着控制自己的坏脾气，这对她来说至关重要。
[01:41.35]conclude v. 断定，推断出；（使）结束；达成， 订立 示例 ① The report concluded that at a ticket price of $50, 000, there could be 500, 000 passengers flying into space each year. 这个报告推断，如果票价为五万美元，每年将有五十万乘客飞到太空旅行。（2006. 12）② It was reported that a trade agreement was concluded between the two countries. 据报道，两国之间签署了贸易协定。
[01:48.99]literal a. 字面意义的；完全按原文的；不夸张的 示例 ① A literal piggy bank of immune cells could one day be transplanted back into humans to boost the aged or fight diseases like HIV. 这种免疫细胞储蓄罐毫不夸张，未来的某一天它能够被移植到人的体内，抗衰老或抵御如艾滋病等疾病。（New Scientist） ② I even have no idea the literal meaning of this word. 我甚至连这个词的字面意思都不知道。
[01:56.63]dedicate v. 把…奉献给；（在书、音乐或作品的前部）题献词；为（建筑物等）举行落成典礼 示例 ① Her blog, she says, is dedicated to sensible parenting. 她说她的博客致力于推广做明智的父母这一概念。（2009. 6）② This novel is dedicated to my dear parents. 谨以此小说献给我亲爱的父母。
[02:04.93]grant v.（尤指正式地或法律上）同意，准予；（勉强）承认‖n.（政府、机构的）拨款，补助金 示例 ① Such programs can be expensive, of course, but cheap compared with the millions already invested in scholarships and grants for kids who have little chance to graduate without special support. 当然这些项目的费用是昂贵的，但是与在没有特别资助就不太可能毕业的孩子们身上投入的数百万奖学金和补助金相比，这已经很便宜了。（2011. 6）② Her boyfriend was always there but she just took him for granted. 她男朋友随叫随到，但她却不把他当回事。
[02:13.53]carbon n. 碳 示例 ① There are many different ways to measure agricultural performance besides food yield: energy use, environmental costs, water purity, carbon footprint and biodiversity. 除了粮食产量，还可以使用很多不同的方法来衡量农业表现：能源利用、 环境成本、水的纯净度、碳排放量和生物多样性。（2008. 12）② Carbon can be found in all living things. 所有生物都含碳元素。
[02:20.47]industrial a. 工业的，产业的；用于工业的；工业发达的 示例 ① Industrial pollution in our town had supposedly turned students into living science experiments breathing in a laboratory's worth of heavy metals like manganese, chromium and nickel each day. 我市工业的污染恐怕已经把学生变成了活生生的科学实验品，每天呼吸这相当于实验室里剂量的锰、铬、镍等重金属。（2009. 12）② There are serious pollution problems in the world's leading industrial nations. 全球主要工业国都存在严重的污染问题。
[02:29.51]hatch v. 孵化；孵出；秘密策划，（尤指）密谋‖n. 舱口；舱门；孵蛋 示例 ① It lays its eggs on their bark, which the larvae, once hatched, bore into and consume the bark, eventually starving the tree of water and nutrients. 它（甲虫）能够在它们（灰树）的树干上产卵，甲虫的幼虫一旦被孵化出来就能够在树干上打洞并消耗其养分，最终将树的水分和营养消耗殆尽。（The Economist） ② He was accused of hatching up an illegal deal with a crime gang. 他被指控与一犯罪团伙密谋非法交易。
[02:35.72]patent n. 专利权‖v. 获得专利权‖a. 有专利的；专利生产的 示例 ① These same universities are also the institutions producing the greatest share of PhD graduates, science citations, patents and licence income. 同样，这些大学也是培养出最多博士生、发表最多科研成果、获得最多专利和特许收入的机构。（2011. 12）② It was a patent lie that he will marry me when he has good money. 当他手头宽裕时就会娶我，这是一个赤裸裸的谎言。
[02:43.22]relief n. 宽慰；（焦虑、痛苦等的）减轻，缓和；救济；救济金 示例 ① According to the weather report, we should have some relief by the end of the week. 天气预报说这个周末（持续高温的）天气会有所缓解。（2009. 6）② Much to my relief I passed the postgraduate entrance examination at last. 令我感到十分欣慰的是，我终于通过了硕士研究生入学考试。
[02:52.94]intact a. 完好无损，完整的 示例 ① Two African countries might have been candidates, Nigeria and South Africa. But only one would keep the acronym intact. 两个非洲国家——尼日利亚和南非都被列为金砖国候选国，但只有一个能使得首字母缩略词“金砖”保持完整。（The Economist）② She emerged from the trial with her property and reputation intact. 她受审获释，财产和名誉丝毫未受损害。
[03:00.67]hint n. 暗示；征兆‖v. 暗示，示意 示例 ① And though Hu Jintao and the rest of the Chinese leadership aren't inclined to lecture visiting Presidents, he might gently hint that Beijing is getting a little nervous about the value of the dollar— which has fallen 15% since March, in large part because of increasing fears that America's debt load is becoming unmanageable. 尽管胡锦涛和其他中国领导人并不愿意对远道而来的总统说教，但是他或许会友善地暗示：北京开始有些担心美元的价值——自从3月份以来，美元已经贬值了 15％，大部分原因是人们越来越担心美国政府的债务管理失控。（2012. 12）② Mary hoped he'd take the hint and love her more and love her long. 玛丽希望他能明白她的意思，爱她多一点，爱她久一点。
[03:09.03]shed n. 棚屋，小屋；厂房‖v. 摆脱，去除； 使脱落；使蜕下 示例 ① The result could be a group of young people that, like their boomer parents, grows up with a strong sense of purpose and sheds the image of apathy they've inherited from Generation X. 其结果可能是：一群年轻人就像二战后出生在生育高峰期的父辈一样，伴随着强烈的使命感长大，并且褪去他们从X一代（指在60年代后期和70年代出生的美国人）继承下来的冷漠形象。（2010. 6）② They were boxed up in a small shed during the flood. 洪水泛滥时他们被困在一间小棚里。
[03:16.01]compensate v. 弥补；补偿，给（某人）赔偿 示例 ① Broadly, the deal provides a mechanism for Google to compensate authors and publishers whose rights it has breached (including giving them a share of any future revenue it generates from their works). 从广义上说，这个协议为谷歌补偿那些被侵权的作家和出版商提供了一种机制（包括分给他们一部分因著作而产生的未来收益）。（2011. 12） ② Nothing can compensate for the loss of true love. 失去真爱是无法弥补的。
[03:24.43]equation n. 方程式，等式；相等；（多种因素的）平衡 示例 ① Einstein discovered to his horror that Hilbert had taken what he had learned from Einstein's lectures and was racing to come up with the correct equations first. 爱因斯坦惊恐地发现，希尔伯特利用从他的讲座中学到的知识正要抢先提出正确的公式。（2007. 12）② There is an equation between unemployment and rising crime levels. 失业人数增加则犯罪数量增加。
[03:32.99]tissue n.（动植物细胞的）组织；纸巾；（用于包装易碎物品的）薄纸 示例 ① When a patient needed a new organ, such as a kidney, the surgeon would contact a commercial organ producer, give him the patient's immunological profile and would then be sent a kidney with the correct tissue type. 当病人需要一个新的器官，例如肾的时候， 外科医生会联系商业器官生产商，给他病人的免疫档案，然后就可以收到组织类型适合的肾。（2008. 6）② She wiped off the sweat from her face with a piece of facial tissue. 她用一张面巾纸擦掉脸上的汗水。
[03:39.56]subtle a. 微妙的；巧妙的；含蓄的 示例 ① Critics point out that, by giving Google the right to commercially exploit its database, the settlement paves the way for a subtle shift in the company's role from provider of information to seller. 批评家指出，通过赋予谷歌从绝版书籍中开发数据库的权利，这一协议为谷歌从信息供应者到信息出售者的微妙转换铺平了道路。（2011. 12） ② There were subtle hints in his letter. 他的信中有些微妙的暗示。
[03:44.48]procedure n. 程序；步骤，手续；手术 示例 ① A specialist who performs a procedure in a 30-minute visit can be paid three times more than a primary care physician using that same 30 minutes to discuss a patient's disease. 一名专科医生耗时30分钟进行某个手术，其收入要比一名花同样多的时间去讨论一个病人病情的初级护理医生高3倍。（2009. 12）② JoД's lawyer told him that making a complaint is quite a simple procedure. 约翰的律师告诉他，申诉的手续相当简单。
[03:53.86]constant a. 连续发生的，不断的；不变的，恒定的 示例 ① We humans, like all warm-blooded animals, can keep our core body temperatures pretty much constant regardless of what's going on in the world around us. 跟所有的温血动物一样，无论外界发生什么变化，我们人类都可以保持身体恒温。（2008. 12）② This old temple attracts a constant stream of visitors all day. 这座古庙一整天都有络绎不绝的游客。
[04:01.04]summit n. 山顶；峰会 示例 ① Population aging is on every agenda, from G8 economic conferences to NATO summits. 从八国首脑经济会议到北大西洋公约组织峰会，人口老龄化都被提上日程。（2010. 12）② They reached the summit of Everest at noon. 他们在中午时分抵达珠穆朗玛峰的峰顶。
[04:06.52]smash v. 打碎；猛烈撞击；撞毁（车辆）‖n. 破碎声；撞碎声；扣球 示例 ① In 2004, NASA scientists announced that there was a chance that Apophis, an asteroid larger than two football fields, could smash into Earth in 2029. 在2004年的时候，美国航空航天局的科学家们宣布，阿波菲斯这个比两个足球场还大的小行星可能会在2029年撞击地球。（Science）② It was reported that youths had broken into the bar and smashed the place up last week. 据报道， 上周一群年轻人闯进酒吧，把里面砸了个乱七八糟。
[04:16.26]county n. （英国、爱尔兰的）郡；（美国等的）县 示例 ① A new, county-by-county analysis of life expectancy in the U.S. shows more than 80 percent of U.S. counties are lagging further behind the world's longest-lived countries in 2007 than they did in 2000. 美国最新一项县级预期寿命分析表明，与2000年相比，2007年美国超过80%的县级居民的预期寿命都进一步低于世界上最长寿的国家。（Discovery） ② He had been to the Orange County when he was a child. 他小时候去过奥兰治县。
