[04:31.62]conduct v. 实施；指挥‖ n. 行为，举止 示例 ① It aims to create yet another generation of people who will conduct dialogue with the imaginary Israel. 它旨在培养出另外一代人，让他们将来和假想中的以色列人展开对话。（The Daily Beast）② She conducted herself far better than expected. 她表现得比预料的要好得多。
[04:39.99]account n. 账户；账目；赊购 示例 ① In still-fertile America it currently accounts for about 40% of total population growth, and in fast-ageing western Europe for about 90%. 在出生率仍较高的美国，目前移民约占总人口增长的 40%，而在人口老龄化迅速的西欧，移民人口大约占总人口增长的90%。（2010. 12） ② The old professor retired early on account of ill health. 那位老教授体弱多病，所以提前退休。
[04:47.02]calorie n. 卡，卡路里 示例 ① Ask anyone why there is an obesity epidemic and they will tell you that it's all down to eating too much and burning too few calories. 随便找个人问问为什么会流行肥胖症，所有人都会告诉你， 那是因为吃得太多，而卡路里消耗太少。（2008. 12）② For beauty of her body, she always counts her calorie of diets. 为了身材好看，她总是控制饮食中的热量。
[04:54.51]startle v. 使惊吓，使大吃一惊 示例 ① They found that varenicline significantly reduced startle reactivity and saccade errors, regardless of subjects' smoking status. 他们发现，不论受试对象的吸烟情况如何，瓦伦尼克林能显著减轻惊跳反应和眼跳跃错误。（www.psychiatryonline.org）② He look at her with startled eyes at the news of her husband's death. 当听到她丈夫的死讯，他吃惊地看着她。
[05:03.71]thoughtful a. 沉思的；体贴的；深思熟虑的 示例 ① Richard Jackson and Neil Howe of America's CSIS, in a thoughtful book called The Graying of the Great Powers, argue that the aging of the developed countries will have a number of serious security implications. 美国国际战略研究中心的理查德·杰克逊和尼尔•豪在一本颇有思想的名为《超级大国老龄化》的书中称，发达国家的人口老龄化问题将带来许多严重的安全隐患。（2010. 12）② It was very thoughtful of you to send the flowers on my birthday. 在我生日那天送花给我，你真体贴。
[05:11.29]fragment n. 碎片，片段‖v. 破裂，分裂，打碎 示例 ① Scientists have picked up fragments of people's thoughts by decoding the brain activity caused by words that they hear. 科学家们已经可以通过分析由所听到的话语引起的大脑活动来获取人们思想的片段。（The Guardian）② Police found fragments of airplane near the crash scene. 警察在坠毁现场找到了飞机的残骸。
[05:20.00]controversial a. 引起争论的，有争议的 示例 ① But Google's book-scanning project is proving controversial. 但是，谷歌的图书扫描项目是有争议的。（2011. 12） ② They tried their best to run away from controversial issues. 他们尽力避开有争议的问题。
[05:26.21]critical a. 批评的；极重要的；危急时刻的；决定性的 示例 ① In addition to pollution and traffic jams, auto safety is a critical issue in developing nations. 除了污染和交通堵塞以外，机动车安全问题也是发展中国家的一个重要的问题。（2008. 12）② According to the latest education reform, students are encouraged to develop critical thinking instead of accepting everything they are told without questioning it. 根据最新的教育改革，要鼓励学生培养批判性思维，而不是不加质疑地全盘接受传授给他们的知识。
